{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483702-does-mage-have-any-kind-of-generic-monster-npc-so-to-speak","id":1483702,"title":"Does mage have any kind of \"generic monster npc\" so to speak","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-11T01:08:34-07:00","id":1483702,"title":"Does mage have any kind of \"generic monster npc\" so to speak","content":"You know like hobgoblins in changeling or pandorans in promethean or chimeras in deviant or cryptids in demon etc...<br /> Those kind of things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T02:00:47-07:00","id":1483708,"title":"","content":"The closest would be Abyssal entities. They directly interact with core mechanics of Mage and are thematically relevant. Mechanically they use twisted ephemeral entity rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T03:01:59-07:00","id":1483710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483702-does-mage-have-any-kind-of-generic-monster-npc-so-to-speak?p=1483708#post1483708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest would be Abyssal entities. They directly interact with core mechanics of Mage and are thematically relevant. Mechanically they use twisted ephemeral entity rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe goetian demons too, in that each of them springs from within the self and mental-spiritual baggage &amp; unconscious of individual awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T09:21:22-07:00","id":1483717,"title":"","content":"Obligatory &quot;Yes. People.&quot; post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T09:53:38-07:00","id":1483718,"title":"","content":"I think Mage has a few different things that fit a similar role, in a manner that kind of belies them being generic.<br /> <br /> Like, if we're just saying things that fit a straightforward monster role, that's Abyssal intruders, the Bound, and Temple Guardians. Yet, none of those things really have the freedom of movement and ubiquity you might get from cryptids and hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> The Awakened aren't really haunted by any specific monster because half of their schtick is to go poking around in all kinds of places and find what's living there, and the other half is that their supernatural quality has a lot of suppression to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T09:53:58-07:00","id":1483719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1483702-does-mage-have-any-kind-of-generic-monster-npc-so-to-speak?p=1483708#post1483708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest would be Abyssal entities. They directly interact with core mechanics of Mage and are thematically relevant. Mechanically they use twisted ephemeral entity rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah with mahe focusing on mysteries and all that i figured there would probably be weird creatures to investigate<br /> Good to know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27340-anyoneatall","name":"Anyoneatall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T06:39:06-07:00","id":1483786,"title":"","content":"The bound as literal magic eaters seem pretty generic, but are likely vanishingly rare and are related to some supernal symbol, making them specific.<br /> <br /> Sleepers, and the lie itself as it is embedded in their souls...<br /> <br /> Abyssal entities are a much better suggestion. And since every mage can he risking paradox, there is always some chance they will show up...but may also be vanishingly rare in conservative groups.<br /> <br /> The Scelesti, again dabbling with the Abyss and most mages would default to treating them as monsters (rather than addicts)...<br /> <br /> But yeah, i think the Abyss is the generic evil in the setting. Scelesti, sleepers, Acamoth and Gulmoth are all just bad for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 06-12-2022, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T13:40:24-07:00","id":1483807,"title":"","content":"Goetia are some that mages tend to interact more with, especially since they are one of the few splats with full access to the Astral. If one is in the Fallen, then something suspicious is going on, like a mage experimenting or having unsafely relinquished a spell upon death.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are the single most common ephemeral being and spirits are fairly common too. They have Numina to communicate without materializing. A type of dog spirit (guard dogs, domestic pet, seeing eye dog) could have Claimed a host by now and just runs into the cabal while on the job (an Abyssal horror could be affecting their human) or looking for a new home. A ghost could be haunting one of the mages' friends and that leads to a greater mystery (like the having been mistaken for a slasher who is now a Geist) and more NPCs. It all depends on where you want the chronicle to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-12-2022, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}